I was able to build the PC overlaid nethack with virtually no hitches.
The development team should be congratulated on a very nice job!

Oh, but there was one hitch.  Running DOS 4.01, if you to do the build with
make45l, there isn't enough memory for the compiler to run!

The solution was fairly obvious, but to save everyone valuable thinking time here
it is:

do a

make45l -n > compile.bat

then edit compile.bat so that it only executes the compile commands (the ones
starting with 'cl').   Then run compile.bat.

Once everything is compiled, you can do a make45l install and you're in
business.

Build time on my 8MHZ AT was in excess of 4 hours.  Having the power to my
house cut out three times didn't help matters :-0

